. 中文长处问卷在青少年群体中应用的信效度. 中国临床心理学杂志, 22(3), 470-474.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref26\", \"unstructured\": \"周林刚, 冯健华(2005). 社会支持理论——一个文献的回顾. 广西师范学院学报, 26(3), 11-14+20.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref27\", \"unstructured\": \"周雅, 刘翔平(2011). 大学生的性格优势及与主观幸福感的关系. 心理发展与教育, 27(5), 536-542.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref28\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1186/1745-6215-15-289\"}, {\"key\": \"ref29\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1177/1049731513477214\"}, {\"key\": \"ref30\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1177/1049731512450074\"}, {\"key\": \"ref31\", \"unstructured\": \"Eleni, P., & Margarita, O. T. (2018). Towards Youth Happiness and Mental Health in the United Arab Emirates: The Path of Character Strengths in a Multicultural Population. Journal of Happiness Studies, 19, 333-350.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref32\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.3389/fpsyg.2017.01159\"}, {\"key\": \"ref33\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.7717/peerj.3396\"}, {\"key\": \"ref34\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1080/17439760.2016.1163403\"}, {\"key\": \"ref35\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1080/17439760701228938\"}, {\"key\": \"ref36\", \"unstructured\": \"Peterson, C., & Seligman, M. (2004). Character Strengths and Virtues: A Handbook and Classification (Vol. 42). American Psychological Association/Oxford University Press.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref37\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1007/s10902-009-9181-2\"}, {\"key\": \"ref38\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.3389/fpsyg.2015.00456\"}, {\"key\": \"ref39\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1556/JBA.1.2012.011\"}, {\"key\": \"ref40\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1037/a0035268\"}], \"container-title\": [\"Advances in Psychology\"], \"original-title\": [\"大学生积极心理品质与心理韧性的关系：社会支持与手机依赖的平行中介作用\"], \"deposited\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 11, 7]], \"date-time\": \"2025-11-07T02:04:08Z\", \"timestamp\": 1762481048000}, \"score\": 95.95251, \"resource\": {\"primary\": {\"URL\": \"https://www.hanspub.org/journal/paperinformation?paperid=77903\"}}, \"issued\": {\"date-parts\": [[2023]]}, \"references-count\": 40, \"journal-issue\": {\"issue\": \"12\", \"published-print\": {\"date-parts\": [[2023]]}}, \"URL\": \"https://doi.org/10.12677/ap.2023.1312797\", \"ISSN\": [\"2160-7273\", \"2160-7281\"], \"issn-type\": [{\"type\": \"print\", \"value\": \"2160-7273\"}, {\"type\": \"electronic\", \"value\": \"2160-7281\"}], \"published\": {\"date-parts\": [[2023]]}}','2026-09-23 12:13:46','therelationshipbetweencollegestudents’positivepsychologicalqualityandpsychologic|2023|欧阳','lit_481fb5ba51c3011b422289f0c862c20a','2026-09-23 12:13:50','2026-09-23 12:13:50'),('10.3389/fpsyt.2025.1572963','10.3389/fpsyt.2025.1572963','Smartphone addiction and academic procrastination among college students: a serial mediation model of self-control and academic self-efficacy','[\"Xiuli Zhao\", \"Huahua Wang\", \"Zaoming Ma\", \"Libing Zhang\"]','Frontiers in Psychiatry',2025,NULL,NULL,NULL,'article','Introduction Researches have highlighted the individual roles of smartphone addiction (SA), self-control (S-C), and academic self-efficacy (AS-E) in predicting academic procrastination (AP), but studies on how these variables combine to affect AP are scarce. Drawing inspiration from the conceptual model of procrastination, this research endeavors to examine a serial mediation model in which SA serves as a precursor, with S-C and AS-E acting as serial mediators in predicting AP among college students who are prone to it. <ja',NULL,'imported','10.3389/fpsyt.2025.1572963','https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyt.2025.1572963',NULL,12,0,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-23 12:13:28','smartphoneaddictionandacademicprocrastinationamongcollegestudents:aserialmediati|2025|zhao','lit_48ceb73c7525c363e2f81b9fa2def539','2026-09-23 12:13:28','2026-09-23 12:13:28'),('10.2139/ssrn.4053961','10.2139/ssrn.4053961','Psychological Well-Being and Social Media Use: A Meta-Analysis of Associations between Social Media Use and Depression, Anxiety, Loneliness, Eudaimonic, Hedonic and Social Well-Being','[\"Jeff Hancock\", \"Sunny Xun Liu\", \"Mufan Luo\", \"Hannah Mieczkowski\"]','SSRN Electronic Journal',2022,NULL,NULL,NULL,'article','（Crossref 未提供摘要，请以原文为准）',NULL,'imported','10.2139/ssrn.4053961','https://doi.org/10.2139/ssrn.4053961',NULL,81,0,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-23 12:13:28','psychologicalwell-beingandsocialmediause:ameta-analysisofassociationsbetweensoci|2022|hancock','lit_4b76e00a227c6d5443a75d0633fe5a0b','2026-09-23 12:13:28','2026-09-23 12:13:28'),('10.51685/jqd.2026.003','10.51685/jqd.2026.003','The relationship between social media use and perceived social support, loneliness, and emotional connection across 7 countries','[\"Brenna Davidson\", \"Nicole Ellison\", \"William Tov\", \"Ryan Ritter\"]','Journal of Quantitative Description: Digital Media',2026,NULL,NULL,NULL,'article','Social media plays a central role in shaping interpersonal connections, yet its association with socioemotional well-being remains widely debated. This study examines the relationship between social media use, loneliness, emotional connection, and perceived social support across seven diverse countries using data from the 2022 Gallup/Meta State of Social Connections Survey. To address inconsistencies in prior research, we employ Specification Curve Analysis (SCA) to assess how different measurements and analytical choices shape how these relationships are reported. Findings suggest lim',NULL,'imported','10.51685/jqd.2026.003','https://doi.org/10.51685/jqd.2026.003',NULL,0,0,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-23 12:13:28','therelationshipbetweensocialmediauseandperceivedsocialsupport,loneliness,andemot|2026|davidson','lit_4f2c0155a0e266409c2cdaaaf5b40d74','2026-09-23 12:13:28','2026-09-23 12:13:28'),('10.21203/rs.3.rs-6871454/v1','10.21203/rs.3.rs-6871454/v1','Unveiling Contributing Pathways to Problematic Mobile Phone Use: Mediating Effects of FOMO, Cyberloafing, Mobile Phone and Social Media Use','[\"Zafer Kadirhan\", \"Yunus Alkis\", \"Berkan Celik\", \"Sacip Toker\", \"Soner Yildirim\"]',NULL,2026,NULL,NULL,NULL,'preprint','<title>Abstract</title>\n                <p>Closely aligned with the pervasive presence of mobile phones in today\'s society surrounded by technology, this study sets out to examine the mediating roles of respect to cyberloafing, fear of missing out (FoMO), mobile phone use hours (MPUH), and social media use hours (SMUH) in the effects of gender and age on problematic mobile phone use (PMPU) among university students. A correlational research method was employed in this study. The participants were 1,272 university students. Data were collected using paper-pencil questionnaires and analyzed through path analysis. The results showed that cyberloafing, FoMO, mobile phone use hours, and social media use hours significantly contributed to the prediction of PMPU. Furthermore, while age indirectly influenced PMPU via FoMO and mobile phone use hours, gender indirectly influenced PMPU via FoMO, cyberloafing, mobile phone use hours, and social media use hours. The study contributes to a deeper understanding of the interactions between psychological reactions and technological behaviors aligns with the broader goal of promoting healthy technology use in educational environments. Insights from this research can inform interventions and policies aimed at fostering responsible and beneficial technology use among students. The implications of this study are multifaceted and can be significant in addressing issues related to PMPU among university students.</p>',NULL,'crossref','10.21203/rs.3.rs-6871454/v1','https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-6871454/v1',NULL,0,1,'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/','{\"institution\": [{\"name\": \"Research Square\"}], \"indexed\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]], \"date-time\": \"2026-02-13T12:27:55Z\", \"timestamp\": 1770985675992, \"version\": \"3.50.1\"}, \"posted\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]]}, \"group-title\": \"In Review\", \"reference-count\": 0, \"publisher\": \"Springer Science and Business Media LLC\", \"license\": [{\"start\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]], \"date-time\": \"2026-02-13T00:00:00Z\", \"timestamp\": 1770940800000}, \"content-version\": \"unspecified\", \"delay-in-days\": 0, \"URL\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\"}], \"content-domain\": {\"domain\": [], \"crossmark-restriction\": false}, \"accepted\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 6, 11]]}, \"DOI\": \"10.21203/rs.3.rs-6871454/v1\", \"type\": \"posted-content\", \"created\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]], \"date-time\": \"2026-02-13T11:51:33Z\", \"timestamp\": 1770983493000}, \"source\": \"Crossref\", \"is-referenced-by-count\": 0, \"title\": [\"Unveiling Contributing Pathways to Problematic Mobile Phone Use: Mediating Effects of FOMO, Cyberloafing, Mobile Phone and Social Media Use\"], \"prefix\": \"10.21203\", \"author\": [{\"given\": \"Zafer\", \"family\": \"Kadirhan\", \"sequence\": \"first\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Ankara University\"}], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Yunus\", \"family\": \"Alkis\", \"sequence\": \"additional\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Middle East Technical University\"}], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Berkan\", \"family\": \"Celik\", \"sequence\": \"additional\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Van Yüzüncü Yıl University\"}], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Sacip\", \"family\": \"Toker\", \"sequence\": \"additional\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Atilim University\"}], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Soner\", \"family\": \"Yildirim\", \"sequence\": \"additional\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Middle East Technical University\"}], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}], \"member\": \"297\", \"link\": [{\"URL\": \"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-6871454/v1\", \"content-type\": \"text/html\", \"content-version\": \"vor\", \"intended-application\": \"text-mining\"}, {\"URL\": \"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-6871454/v1.html\", \"content-type\": \"unspecified\", \"content-version\": \"vor\", \"intended-application\": \"similarity-checking\"}], \"deposited\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]], \"date-time\": \"2026-02-13T11:51:39Z\", \"timestamp\": 1770983499000}, \"score\": 27.859293, \"resource\": {\"primary\": {\"URL\": \"https://www.researchsquare.com/article/rs-6871454/v1\"}}, \"issued\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]]}, \"references-count\": 0, \"URL\": \"https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-6871454/v1\", \"published\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 2, 13]]}, \"subtype\": \"preprint\"}','2026-09-23 12:14:02','unveilingcontributingpathwaystoproblematicmobilephoneuse:mediatingeffectsoffomo,|2026|kadirhan','lit_646573c1c5521ade083e7d8cf27c77cf','2026-09-23 12:14:04','2026-09-23 12:14:04'),('10.3389/fpubh.2026.1879219','10.3389/fpubh.2026.1879219','Health correlates and health-related outcomes associated with smartphone-related addictive behaviors in older adults: a scoping review.','[\"Jiang N\", \"Yao J\", \"Wu Y\"]',NULL,2026,NULL,NULL,'1879219','article','<h4>Background</h4>Smartphones support communication, access to services, and social participation in later life, but a small and growing evidence base addresses patterns of use characterised by loss of control and functional interference among older adults.<h4>Objective</h4>To map the concepts, assessment tools, health correlates, and nursing-care implications reported for smartphone-related addictive behaviors in adults aged 60 years or older.<h4>Methods</h4>A scoping review was conducted in accordance with Joanna Briggs Institute guidance and reported with the PRISMA extension for Scoping Reviews. PubMed, Embase, CINAHL, Web of Science, Cochrane Library, CNKI, Wanfang, VIP, and SinoMed were searched from inception to 3 June 2026, and the reference lists of included studies were screened. Eligible original studies involved adults aged 60 years or older and examined smartphone addiction, mobile phone dependence, problematic smartphone or mobile phone use, smartphone overdependence, or short-video-related addictive behaviors primarily undertaken through smartphones. Evidence was synthesized descriptively and interpreted according to study design, measurement applicability, and directness to nursing care.<h4>Results</h4>Twenty-two studies were included: 18 cross-sectional studies, 2 longitudinal studies, 1 randomized controlled trial, and 1 qualitative study. Concepts and measures were heterogeneous. Evidence was most concentrated for associations with poorer sleep quality, depressive symptoms, anxiety, and loneliness. Evidence concerning physical activity, instrumental activities of daily living, posture, visual fatigue, and social participation was more limited. Cognitive evidence was insufficient to support claims of decline. Direct intervention evidence was restricted to one small randomized trial reporting improvements in posture and neck function after home-based corrective exercise. The evidence base was geographically concentrated in China and other Asian settings, and age-stratified findings for the oldest-old were rarely reported.<h4>Conclusion</h4>Current evidence supports cautious clinical inquiry, assessment of problematic use, and balanced health education rather than formal screening or definitive intervention recommendations. Future work should validate later-life-specific definitions and assessment thresholds, use prospective multicenter designs, report age-subgroup findings, and test nursing-led interventions that measure both behavioral and health-related outcomes.','eng','europepmc','42601935','https://europepmc.org/article/MED/42601935',NULL,0,1,'cc by','{\"id\": \"42601935\", \"source\": \"MED\", \"pmid\": \"42601935\", \"pmcid\": \"PMC13472799\", \"fullTextIdList\": {\"fullTextId\": [\"PMC13472799\"]}, \"doi\": \"10.3389/fpubh.2026.1879219\", \"title\": \"Health correlates and health-related outcomes associated with smartphone-related addictive behaviors in older adults: a scoping review.\", \"authorString\": \"Jiang N, Yao J, Wu Y.\", \"authorList\": {\"author\": [{\"fullName\": \"Jiang N\", \"lastName\": \"Jiang\", \"firstName\": \"Nan\", \"initials\": \"N\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of Nursing, Shaanxi University of Chinese Medicine, Xianyang, Shaanxi, China.\"}]}}, {\"fullName\": \"Yao J\", \"lastName\": \"Yao\", \"firstName\": \"Jie\", \"initials\": \"J\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of Nursing, Shaanxi University of Chinese Medicine, Xianyang, Shaanxi, China.\"}]}}, {\"fullName\": \"Wu Y\", \"lastName\": \"Wu\", \"firstName\": \"Yuchen\", \"initials\": \"Y\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of Nursing, Shaanxi University of Chinese Medicine, Xianyang, Shaanxi, China.\"}]}}]}, \"dataLinksTagsList\": {\"dataLinkstag\": [\"supporting_data\"]}, \"journalInfo\": {\"volume\": \"14\", \"journalIssueId\": 4110762, \"dateOfPublication\": \"2026 \", \"monthOfPublication\": 0, \"yearOfPublication\": 2026, \"journal\": {\"medlineAbbreviation\": \"Front Public Health\", \"title\": \"Frontiers in public health\", \"essn\": \"2296-2565\", \"issn\": \"2296-2565\", \"nlmid\": \"101616579\", \"isoabbreviation\": \"Front Public Health\"}, \"printPublicationDate\": \"2026-01-01\"}, \"pubYear\": \"2026\", \"pageInfo\": \"1879219\", \"affiliation\": \"School of Nursing, Shaanxi University of Chinese Medicine, Xianyang, Shaanxi, China.\", \"publicationStatus\": \"epublish\", \"language\": \"eng\", \"pubModel\": \"Electronic-eCollection\", \"pubTypeList\": {\"pubType\": [\"Scoping Review\", \"systematic-review\", \"Journal Article\"]}, \"meshHeadingList\": {\"meshHeading\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Humans\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Behavior, Addictive\", \"meshQualifierList\": {\"meshQualifier\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"EP\", \"qualifierName\": \"epidemiology\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"PX\", \"qualifierName\": \"psychology\"}]}}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Aged\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Middle Aged\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Smartphone\"}]}, \"keywordList\": {\"keyword\": [\"Nursing care\", \"Older Adults\", \"Scoping Review\", \"Problematic Smartphone Use\", \"Short-video Overuse\", \"Smartphone-related Addictive Behaviors\"]}, \"subsetList\": {\"subset\": [{\"code\": \"IM\", \"name\": \"Index Medicus\"}]}, \"fullTextUrlList\": {\"fullTextUrl\": [{\"availability\": \"Subscription required\", \"availabilityCode\": \"S\", \"documentStyle\": \"doi\", \"site\": \"DOI\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpubh.2026.1879219\"}, {\"availability\": \"Open access\", \"availabilityCode\": \"OA\", \"documentStyle\": \"html\", \"site\": \"Europe_PMC\", \"url\": \"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13472799\"}, {\"availability\": \"Open access\", \"availabilityCode\": \"OA\", \"documentStyle\": \"pdf\", \"site\": \"Europe_PMC\", \"url\": \"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13472799?pdf=render\"}]}, \"isOpenAccess\": \"Y\", \"inEPMC\": \"Y\", \"inPMC\": \"Y\", \"citedByCount\": 0, \"hasReferences\": \"Y\", \"hasTextMinedTerms\": \"Y\", \"hasDbCrossReferences\": \"N\", \"hasPDF\": \"Y\", \"hasBook\": \"N\", \"hasSuppl\": \"Y\", \"hasLabsLinks\": \"N\", \"hasData\": \"Y\", \"license\": \"cc by\", \"authMan\": \"N\", \"epmcAuthMan\": \"N\", \"nihAuthMan\": \"N\", \"hasTMAccessionNumbers\": \"Y\", \"tmAccessionTypeList\": {\"accessionType\": [\"doi\"]}, \"dateOfCompletion\": \"2026-08-15\", \"dateOfCreation\": \"2026-08-15\", \"dateOfRevision\": \"2026-09-01\", \"electronicPublicationDate\": \"2026-07-31\", \"firstPublicationDate\": \"2026-07-31\", \"firstIndexDate\": \"2026-08-16\", \"fullTextReceivedDate\": \"2026-09-09\", \"hasEvaluations\": \"N\"}','2026-09-23 12:14:04','healthcorrelatesandhealth-relatedoutcomesassociatedwithsmartphone-relatedaddicti|2026|n','lit_6af50bea6546792d37624df69ef50ddb','2026-09-23 12:14:04','2026-09-23 12:14:04'),('10.12677/ass.2020.92029','10.12677/ass.2020.92029','The Influence of High School Students’ Social Support on Social Adaptation—The Role of Self-Identity','[\"晓雪 张\"]','Advances in Social Sciences',2020,'09','02','179-187','article',NULL,NULL,'crossref','10.12677/ass.2020.92029','https://doi.org/10.12677/ass.2020.92029',NULL,1,0,NULL,'{\"indexed\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 11, 21]], \"date-time\": \"2025-11-21T03:55:36Z\", \"timestamp\": 1763697336526, \"version\": \"3.45.0\"}, \"reference-count\": 11, \"publisher\": \"Hans Publishers\", \"issue\": \"02\", \"content-domain\": {\"domain\": [], \"crossmark-restriction\": false}, \"short-container-title\": [\"ASS\"], \"published-print\": {\"date-parts\": [[2020]]}, \"DOI\": \"10.12677/ass.2020.92029\", \"type\": \"journal-article\", \"created\": {\"date-parts\": [[2020, 2, 19]], \"date-time\": \"2020-02-19T00:59:49Z\", \"timestamp\": 1582073989000}, \"page\": \"179-187\", \"source\": \"Crossref\", \"is-referenced-by-count\": 1, \"title\": [\"The Influence of High School Students’ Social Support on Social Adaptation—The Role of Self-Identity\"], \"prefix\": \"10.12677\", \"volume\": \"09\", \"author\": [{\"given\": \"晓雪\", \"family\": \"张\", \"sequence\": \"first\", \"affiliation\": [], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}], \"member\": \"4945\", \"reference\": [{\"key\": \"ref1\", \"unstructured\": \"李文道, 邹泓, 赵霞. 初中生的社会支持与学校适应的关系[J]. 心理发展与教育, 2003, 19(3): 73-81.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref2\", \"unstructured\": \"[美]埃里克•H•埃里克森. 同一性: 青少年与危机[M]. 孙名之, 译. 杭州: 浙江教育出版社, 1998.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref3\", \"unstructured\": \"张炜. 青少年中期自我同一性发展特征与社会适应行为的关系[D]: [硕士学位论文]. 武汉: 华中师范大学, 2007.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref4\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"crossref\", \"unstructured\": \"黄华华, 刘少英, 徐芬. 大学生的自我同一性与社会适应[J]. 中国心理卫生杂志, 2014, 28(1): 70-74.\", \"DOI\": \"10.14725/gjpr.v3n2a1132\"}, {\"key\": \"ref5\", \"unstructured\": \"刘锐. 大学生自我同一性与人际适应相互关系研究[J]. 社会心理科学, 2014, 29(1): 14-18.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref6\", \"unstructured\": \"田晓峰. 盘锦市寄宿制高中新生的学校适应和心理健康状况调查及干预的研究[D]: [硕士学位论文]. 大连: 辽宁师范大学, 2011.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref7\", \"unstructured\": \"程虹娟, 张春和, 龚永辉. 大学生社会支持的研究综述[J]. 成都理工大学学报(社会科学版), 2004, 12(1): 88-91.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref8\", \"unstructured\": \"叶悦妹, 戴晓阳. 大学生社会支持评定量表的编制[J]. 中国临床心理学杂志, 2008, 16(5): 456-458.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref9\", \"unstructured\": \"余益兵, 邹泓, 周晖, 等. 青少年社会适应状况评估问卷的编制[C]//中国心理学会. 第十二届全国心理学学术大会论文摘要集. 北京: 中国心理学会, 2009: 96-97.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref10\", \"unstructured\": \"郭金山, 车文博. 自我同一性与相关概念的辨析[J]. 心理科学, 2004, 27(5): 1266-1267+1250.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref11\", \"unstructured\": \"周浩, 龙立荣. 共同方法偏差的统计检验与控制方法[J]. 心理科学进展, 2004, 12(6): 942-94.\"}], \"container-title\": [\"Advances in Social Sciences\"], \"original-title\": [\"高中生社会支持对社会适应的影响——自我同一性的作用\"], \"deposited\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 11, 21]], \"date-time\": \"2025-11-21T03:15:59Z\", \"timestamp\": 1763694959000}, \"score\": 104.99152, \"resource\": {\"primary\": {\"URL\": \"https://www.hanspub.org/journal/paperinformation?paperid=34230\"}}, \"issued\": {\"date-parts\": [[2020]]}, \"references-count\": 11, \"journal-issue\": {\"issue\": \"02\", \"published-print\": {\"date-parts\": [[2020]]}}, \"URL\": \"https://doi.org/10.12677/ass.2020.92029\", \"ISSN\": [\"2169-2556\", \"2169-2564\"], \"issn-type\": [{\"type\": \"print\", \"value\": \"2169-2556\"}, {\"type\": \"electronic\", \"value\": \"2169-2564\"}], \"published\": {\"date-parts\": [[2020]]}}','2026-09-23 12:13:46','theinfluenceofhighschoolstudents’socialsupportonsocialadaptation—theroleofself-i|2020|张','lit_751c44a8e1f971f973eff9ba178f71ee','2026-09-23 12:13:50','2026-09-23 12:13:50'),('10.3389/fpubh.2026.1894257','10.3389/fpubh.2026.1894257','The chain mediation effect of self-regulation and pre-sleep smartphone use on the relationship between smartphone dependence and bedtime procrastination among college students.','[\"Liu W\", \"Yuan Z\", \"Li S\", \"Chen Y\", \"Liu H\"]',NULL,2026,NULL,NULL,'1894257','article','Smartphone dependence and bedtime procrastination are prevalent behavioral issues among college students, yet the psychological mechanisms linking them remain underexplored. This study investigated the chain mediating roles of self-regulation and pre-sleep smartphone use in the relationship between smartphone dependence and bedtime procrastination. A sample of 1,482 Chinese college students completed validated measures of smartphone dependence, self-regulation, pre-sleep smartphone use, and bedtime procrastination. Structural equation modeling and bootstrap analyses (5,000 resamples) were employed, controlling for gender and academic year. Results revealed that smartphone dependence positively predicted bedtime procrastination (standardized total effect of 0.56; direct effect of 0.21, <i>p</i> < 0.001). Both self-regulation and pre-sleep smartphone use served as significant independent mediators. More importantly, the serial mediation pathway-smartphone dependence → self-regulation → pre-sleep smartphone use → bedtime procrastination-was also significant, with a total indirect effect; the aggregate total indirect effect across all three mediation pathways was 0.35. Critically, the serial indirect pathway-smartphone dependence → self-regulation → pre-sleep smartphone use → bedtime procrastination-was statistically significant with a modest standardized coefficient of 0.07. Robustness checks supported the stability of the model. Multi-group analyses further showed that the path from smartphone dependence to pre-sleep smartphone use was stronger among female students than among male students (β = 0.55 vs. β = 0.42), whereas the effects of smartphone dependence on self-regulation (β = -0.35 vs. β = -0.15) and pre-sleep smartphone use (β = 0.60 vs. β = 0.40) were stronger among lower-grade students than among higher-grade students. These findings clarify the multi-path behavioral mechanism from smartphone dependence to bedtime procrastination, highlighting self-regulation and pre-sleep smartphone use as critical intervention targets. Limitations include cross-sectional design and self-report data, warranting future longitudinal and objective assessments.','eng','europepmc','42614735','https://europepmc.org/article/MED/42614735',NULL,0,1,'cc by','{\"id\": \"42614735\", \"source\": \"MED\", \"pmid\": \"42614735\", \"pmcid\": \"PMC13482389\", \"fullTextIdList\": {\"fullTextId\": [\"PMC13482389\"]}, \"doi\": \"10.3389/fpubh.2026.1894257\", \"title\": \"The chain mediation effect of self-regulation and pre-sleep smartphone use on the relationship between smartphone dependence and bedtime procrastination among college students.\", \"authorString\": \"Liu W, Yuan Z, Li S, Chen Y, Liu H.\", \"authorList\": {\"author\": [{\"fullName\": \"Liu W\", \"lastName\": \"Liu\", \"firstName\": \"Wangqing\", \"initials\": \"W\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of National Defense Education and Targeted Training, Jiangsu Maritime Institute, Nanjing, China.\"}]}}, {\"fullName\": \"Yuan Z\", \"lastName\": \"Yuan\", \"firstName\": \"Zhou\", \"initials\": \"Z\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of National Defense Education and Targeted Training, Jiangsu Maritime Institute, Nanjing, China.\"}]}}, {\"fullName\": \"Li S\", \"lastName\": \"Li\", \"firstName\": \"Shangfu\", \"initials\": \"S\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of National Defense Education and Targeted Training, Jiangsu Maritime Institute, Nanjing, China.\"}]}}, {\"fullName\": \"Chen Y\", \"lastName\": \"Chen\", \"firstName\": \"Yun\", \"initials\": \"Y\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"School of Intelligent Control, Changzhou Institute of Industrial Technology, Changzhou, China.\"}]}}, {\"fullName\": \"Liu H\", \"lastName\": \"Liu\", \"firstName\": \"Hangjiang\", \"initials\": \"H\", \"authorAffiliationDetailsList\": {\"authorAffiliation\": [{\"affiliation\": \"Qiaoxing School of Economics and Management, Fujian Normal University of Technology, Fuzhou, China.\"}]}}]}, \"dataLinksTagsList\": {\"dataLinkstag\": [\"supporting_data\"]}, \"journalInfo\": {\"volume\": \"14\", \"journalIssueId\": 4110762, \"dateOfPublication\": \"2026 \", \"monthOfPublication\": 0, \"yearOfPublication\": 2026, \"journal\": {\"medlineAbbreviation\": \"Front Public Health\", \"title\": \"Frontiers in public health\", \"essn\": \"2296-2565\", \"issn\": \"2296-2565\", \"nlmid\": \"101616579\", \"isoabbreviation\": \"Front Public Health\"}, \"printPublicationDate\": \"2026-01-01\"}, \"pubYear\": \"2026\", \"pageInfo\": \"1894257\", \"affiliation\": \"School of National Defense Education and Targeted Training, Jiangsu Maritime Institute, Nanjing, China.\", \"publicationStatus\": \"epublish\", \"language\": \"eng\", \"pubModel\": \"Electronic-eCollection\", \"pubTypeList\": {\"pubType\": [\"research-article\", \"Journal Article\"]}, \"meshHeadingList\": {\"meshHeading\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Humans\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Sleep\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Students\", \"meshQualifierList\": {\"meshQualifier\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"PX\", \"qualifierName\": \"psychology\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"SN\", \"qualifierName\": \"statistics & numerical data\"}]}}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Universities\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Adolescent\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"China\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Female\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Male\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Young Adult\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Smartphone\", \"meshQualifierList\": {\"meshQualifier\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"SN\", \"qualifierName\": \"statistics & numerical data\"}]}}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"descriptorName\": \"Surveys and Questionnaires\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Self-Control\", \"meshQualifierList\": {\"meshQualifier\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"PX\", \"qualifierName\": \"psychology\"}]}}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Procrastination\"}, {\"majorTopic_YN\": \"Y\", \"descriptorName\": \"Internet Addiction Disorder\", \"meshQualifierList\": {\"meshQualifier\": [{\"majorTopic_YN\": \"N\", \"abbreviation\": \"PX\", \"qualifierName\": \"psychology\"}]}}]}, \"keywordList\": {\"keyword\": [\"Self-regulation\", \"Smartphone Dependence\", \"Bedtime Procrastination\", \"Chain Mediation Model\", \"Pre-sleep Smartphone Use\"]}, \"subsetList\": {\"subset\": [{\"code\": \"IM\", \"name\": \"Index Medicus\"}]}, \"fullTextUrlList\": {\"fullTextUrl\": [{\"availability\": \"Subscription required\", \"availabilityCode\": \"S\", \"documentStyle\": \"doi\", \"site\": \"DOI\", \"url\": \"https://doi.org/10.3389/fpubh.2026.1894257\"}, {\"availability\": \"Open access\", \"availabilityCode\": \"OA\", \"documentStyle\": \"html\", \"site\": \"Europe_PMC\", \"url\": \"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13482389\"}, {\"availability\": \"Open access\", \"availabilityCode\": \"OA\", \"documentStyle\": \"pdf\", \"site\": \"Europe_PMC\", \"url\": \"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13482389?pdf=render\"}]}, \"isOpenAccess\": \"Y\", \"inEPMC\": \"Y\", \"inPMC\": \"Y\", \"citedByCount\": 0, \"hasReferences\": \"Y\", \"hasTextMinedTerms\": \"Y\", \"hasDbCrossReferences\": \"N\", \"hasPDF\": \"Y\", \"hasBook\": \"N\", \"hasSuppl\": \"Y\", \"hasLabsLinks\": \"N\", \"hasData\": \"Y\", \"license\": \"cc by\", \"authMan\": \"N\", \"epmcAuthMan\": \"N\", \"nihAuthMan\": \"N\", \"hasTMAccessionNumbers\": \"Y\", \"tmAccessionTypeList\": {\"accessionType\": [\"doi\"]}, \"dateOfCompletion\": \"2026-08-19\", \"dateOfCreation\": \"2026-08-19\", \"dateOfRevision\": \"2026-08-20\", \"electronicPublicationDate\": \"2026-08-04\", \"firstPublicationDate\": \"2026-08-04\", \"firstIndexDate\": \"2026-08-22\", \"fullTextReceivedDate\": \"2026-09-09\", \"hasEvaluations\": \"N\"}','2026-09-23 12:14:04','thechainmediationeffectofself-regulationandpre-sleepsmartphoneuseontherelationsh|2026|w','lit_78c03287017c2b844f4fa45fa494a2e9','2026-09-23 12:14:04','2026-09-23 12:14:04'),('10.31234/osf.io/cdg73','10.31234/osf.io/cdg73','Adolescents\' digital nightlife: The comparative effects of day- and nighttime smartphone use on sleep quality','[\"Teun Siebers\", \"Ine Beyens\", \"Susanne Baumgartner\", \"Patti M. Valkenburg\"]','（期刊信息待补充）',2023,NULL,NULL,NULL,'article','The smartphone occupies a substantial part of adolescents’ daily life, from the moment they wake up to, for some, well beyond their bedtime. The current study compared the impact of adolescents’ daytime, pre-bedtime, and post-bedtime smartphone use on their sleep quality. In addition, it explored the differential effects of lean-back and lean-forward smartphone apps. We collected data from 155 adolescents across 21 days using smartphone tracking (745,706 app activities) in combination with experience sampling (1,950 sleep quality assessments). We found no significant effects of daytime and',NULL,'imported','10.31234/osf.io/cdg73','https://doi.org/10.31234/osf.io/cdg73',NULL,4,0,NULL,NULL,'2026-09-23 12:13:28','adolescents\'digitalnightlife:thecomparativeeffectsofday-andnighttimesmartphoneus|2023|siebers','lit_806f6111c3f69acc9d6f20f416ca9b18','2026-09-23 12:13:28','2026-09-23 12:13:28'),('10.59825/jet.2025.3.2.1','10.59825/jet.2025.3.2.1','The Impact of Mindfulness Sandplay Therapy on Social Self-Efficacy and Smartphone Social Media Dependence among Pre-service Teachers: An Intervention Study','[\"Jing Huang\", \"Xinran Xie\", \"Qiufeng Lin\", \"Heng Huang\", \"Shiqi Huang\", \"Caihong Zhou\"]','Yixin Publisher',2025,'3','2','1-12','article','<jats:p>本研究旨在探讨正念冥想结合团体沙盘游戏对高校师范生手机社交媒体依赖和社会自我效能感的干预效果。研究对象为24 名被试，均分为实验组和对照组，对实验组开展正念冥想结合团体沙盘的干预，对照组不采取任何措施。干预前后分别采用《大学生手机社交媒体依赖问卷》与《大学生社会自我效能感问卷》进行施测，运用SPSS 对两个问卷的总分结果进行分析，研究显示实验组被试社会自我效能感问卷后测结果显著高于前测，手机社交媒体依赖问卷后测结果显著低于前测，实验组、对照组手机社交媒体依赖问卷干预后得分无显著差异。结果表明，正念冥想结合团体沙盘游戏的心理干预方法能有效改善高校师范生的手机社交媒体依赖和提升其社会自我效能感。</jats:p>',NULL,'crossref','10.59825/jet.2025.3.2.1','https://doi.org/10.59825/jet.2025.3.2.1',NULL,0,0,NULL,'{\"indexed\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 3, 27]], \"date-time\": \"2025-03-27T04:07:35Z\", \"timestamp\": 1743048455195, \"version\": \"3.40.3\"}, \"reference-count\": 0, \"publisher\": \"Yixin Publisher\", \"issue\": \"2\", \"content-domain\": {\"domain\": [], \"crossmark-restriction\": false}, \"short-container-title\": [\"Yixin Publisher\"], \"published-print\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 2, 28]]}, \"DOI\": \"10.59825/jet.2025.3.2.1\", \"type\": \"journal-article\", \"created\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 3, 26]], \"date-time\": \"2025-03-26T06:49:22Z\", \"timestamp\": 1742971762000}, \"page\": \"1-12\", \"source\": \"Crossref\", \"is-referenced-by-count\": 0, \"title\": [\"The Impact of Mindfulness Sandplay Therapy on Social Self-Efficacy and Smartphone Social Media Dependence among Pre-service Teachers: An Intervention Study\"], \"prefix\": \"10.59825\", \"volume\": \"3\", \"author\": [{\"given\": \"Jing\", \"family\": \"Huang\", \"sequence\": \"first\", \"affiliation\": [], \"role\": [{\"role\": \"author\", \"vocabulary\": \"crossref\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Xinran\", \"family\": \"Xie\", \"sequence\": \"first\", \"affiliation\": [], \"role\": [{\"role\