持与手机依赖的关系研究. 吉林工商学院学报, (4), 91-93.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref7\", \"unstructured\": \"肖水源(1994). 《社会支持评定量表》的理论基础与研究应用. 临床精神医学杂志, 4(2), 98-100.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref8\", \"unstructured\": \"熊婕, 周宗奎, 陈武, 游志麒, 翟紫艳(2012). 大学生手机成瘾倾向量表的编制. 中国心理卫生杂志, 26(3), 222-225.\"}, {\"key\": \"ref9\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1080/1369118X.2020.1749698\"}, {\"key\": \"ref10\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1089/cpb.2005.8.39\"}, {\"key\": \"ref11\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.2174/157340012803520522\"}, {\"key\": \"ref12\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1176/appi.ajp.2007.07101556\"}, {\"key\": \"ref13\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1016/j.chb.2015.10.030\"}, {\"key\": \"ref14\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1016/S0747-5632(00)00041-8\"}, {\"key\": \"ref15\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1371/journal.pone.0098312\"}, {\"key\": \"ref16\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1186/s12888-016-1083-3\"}, {\"key\": \"ref17\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"crossref\", \"unstructured\": \"Rosenberg, M. (1965). Rosenberg Self-Esteem Scale (RSE). Ac-ceptance and Commitment Therapy. Measures Package, 61, 18.\", \"DOI\": \"10.1037/t01038-000\"}, {\"key\": \"ref18\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1186/1471-2458-11-66\"}, {\"key\": \"ref19\", \"doi-asserted-by\": \"publisher\", \"DOI\": \"10.1186/s12887-019-1699-9\"}], \"container-title\": [\"Advances in Psychology\"], \"original-title\": [\"大学生社会支持、自尊与手机依赖的关系探究\"], \"deposited\": {\"date-parts\": [[2025, 11, 19]], \"date-time\": \"2025-11-19T01:42:54Z\", \"timestamp\": 1763516574000}, \"score\": 120.59269, \"resource\": {\"primary\": {\"URL\": \"https://www.hanspub.org/journal/paperinformation?paperid=57366\"}}, \"issued\": {\"date-parts\": [[2022]]}, \"references-count\": 19, \"journal-issue\": {\"issue\": \"10\", \"published-print\": {\"date-parts\": [[2022]]}}, \"URL\": \"https://doi.org/10.12677/ap.2022.1210439\", \"ISSN\": [\"2160-7273\", \"2160-7281\"], \"issn-type\": [{\"type\": \"print\", \"value\": \"2160-7273\"}, {\"type\": \"electronic\", \"value\": \"2160-7281\"}], \"published\": {\"date-parts\": [[2022]]}}','2026-09-23 12:13:46','therelationshipbetweencollegestudents’socialsupport,self-esteem,andmobilephonede|2022|杜','lit_ecbd96c531d64bd5afa0bb3fbc79eb5a','2026-09-23 12:13:50','2026-09-23 12:13:50'),('10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1752086','10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1752086','Social exclusion and mobile phone dependence in college students: a moderated mediation model of self-control and social self-efficacy','[\"Li Lv\", \"Jialin Huang\", \"Yingchun Cao\"]','Frontiers in Psychology',2026,'17',NULL,NULL,'article','<jats:p>This study integrated Compensatory Internet Use Theory with the I-PACE model to examine a moderated mediation model, aiming to understand the psychological processes linking social exclusion and mobile phone dependence among college students. A cross-sectional survey of 438 Chinese college students (after data cleaning) using validated scales revealed three key findings: First, social exclusion was positively associated with mobile phone dependence; Second, self-control partially mediated this association. Third, social self-efficacy moderated both the direct link between social exclusion and dependence and the first stage of the mediating pathway (from social exclusion to self-control). Consistent with the Expectancy Violation Theory, the positive correlation between social exclusion and mobile phone dependence was stronger among students with higher (vs. lower) social self-efficacy. These findings reveal complex mechanisms underlying mobile phone dependence, highlighting the mediating role of self-control and the counter-amplifying effect of social self-efficacy. Thus, while self-control training may offer broad benefits, tailored interventions should be designed for individuals with high social self-efficacy. Such interventions should guide their social confidence toward repairing offline relationships rather than retreating into online compensatory behaviors.</jats:p>',NULL,'crossref','10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1752086','https://doi.org/10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1752086',NULL,1,1,'https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/','{\"indexed\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 8, 18]], \"date-time\": \"2026-08-18T04:27:29Z\", \"timestamp\": 1787027249210, \"version\": \"build-2736575974\"}, \"reference-count\": 56, \"publisher\": \"Frontiers Media SA\", \"license\": [{\"start\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 4, 13]], \"date-time\": \"2026-04-13T00:00:00Z\", \"timestamp\": 1776038400000}, \"content-version\": \"vor\", \"delay-in-days\": 0, \"URL\": \"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/\"}], \"content-domain\": {\"domain\": [\"frontiersin.org\"], \"crossmark-restriction\": true}, \"short-container-title\": [\"Front. Psychol.\"], \"DOI\": \"10.3389/fpsyg.2026.1752086\", \"type\": \"journal-article\", \"created\": {\"date-parts\": [[2026, 4, 13]], \"date-time\": \"2026-04-13T05:47:32Z\", \"timestamp\": 1776059252000}, \"update-policy\": \"https://doi.org/10.3389/crossmark-policy\", \"source\": \"Crossref\", \"is-referenced-by-count\": 1, \"title\": [\"Social exclusion and mobile phone dependence in college students: a moderated mediation model of self-control and social self-efficacy\"], \"prefix\": \"10.3389\", \"volume\": \"17\", \"author\": [{\"given\": \"Li\", \"family\": \"Lv\", \"sequence\": \"first\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Department of Psychology, School of Normal, Hubei University\", \"place\": [\"Wuhan, China\"]}], \"role\": [{\"vocabulary\": \"crossref\", \"role\": \"author\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Jialin\", \"family\": \"Huang\", \"sequence\": \"additional\", \"affiliation\": [{\"name\": \"Department of Psychology, School of Normal, Hubei University\", \"place\": [\"Wuhan, China\"]}], \"role\": [{\"vocabulary\": \"crossref\", \"role\": \"author\"}]}, {\"given\": \"Yingchun\", \"family\": \"Cao\"